  "notes": "USAGE: {火傷|やけど} can be used as a noun or with する as a suru-verb ({火傷|やけど}する = to get burned).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{火傷|やけど}をする (to get a burn)\n・{火傷|やけど}を{負|お}う (to sustain a burn - formal)\n・{火傷|やけど}が{治|なお}る (the burn heals)\n・{火傷|やけど}の{跡|あと} (burn scar)\n\nSEVERITY LEVELS:\n・{軽度|けいど}の{火傷|やけど} (minor burn)\n・{重度|じゅうど}の{火傷|やけど} (severe burn)\n\nWARNING: For serious burns, seek medical attention. The expression {火傷|やけど}の{功名|こうみょう} (lit. success from getting burned) means achieving something through a mistake or failure.",
